    "description": {
      "value": "<p>High in the mountains, where the air is thin and the wind never stops, Goliath clans live by competition: every hunt, climb, and supper is a chance to outdo yesterday. Fenari who settle among them take to this with enthusiasm, if not always with dignity.</p><p>Over the generations these Fenari grow larger and stockier than any of their kin. Their fur thickens against the cold, often in stone grays and snowy whites, and the bravest of them learn to swell to their hosts' size when it counts.</p><p>Goliath Fenari keep careful score of everything: the heaviest stone lifted, the steepest climb, the most impressive thing found in someone else's pack. They're fiercely proud of their place in the clan and will cheerfully challenge creatures three times their size to prove they deserve it. They tend toward lawful neutral.</p><p><strong>Size.</strong> Living among Goliaths has made these Fenari larger than their kin, most growing between 4'8\" and 5'6\" tall and weighing 100 to 150 pounds. Your size is Medium.</p><p><strong>Languages.</strong> Most Goliath Fenari learn Giant.</p><h3>Goliath Culture Traits</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>Traits</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Compact Power, Mountain Born</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Keeping Score</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Growth Spurt</td></tr></tbody></table>",
      "chat": ""
    },
